# Practice Assignment pages

Student-facing Practice specs. Copy from `templates/Practice Assignment.md` into `Module NN - Topic/Practice (Module N - Topic).md`. Match polished Practices such as Module 2 (flat) or Module 3 (sections).

## Sources

Module topic/MLOs, existing problem bank (if rewriting), Course Map Practice row, and Instructor Notes for classroom50 / accept links.

## Fill rules

| Placeholder | Value |
|-------------|--------|
| `{{N}}` / `{{Topic}}` | Module number and short title |
| `{{OVERVIEW_FOCUS}}` | Short phrase after "programs" (e.g. ` using conditionals and functions`) |
| `{{COMPLETE_LIST}}` | Bullets matching the choice pattern (see below) |
| `{{WALKTHROUGH_VIDEO}}` | Embed/link, or `*[Insert walkthrough video about completing programming assignments]*` |
| `{{ACCEPT_LINK}}` | classroom50 / Classroom accept URL, or `[INSERT ASSIGNMENT LINK]` |
| `{{REQUIREMENTS_LIST}}` | Same choose bullets as Overview (shared bullets stay in the template) |
| `{{FILE_TABLE_ROWS}}` | `\| Problem Title \| \`file.py\` \|` using the **actual** problem titles |
| `{{PROGRAMMING_PROBLEMS}}` | Flat list or sectioned OR list; see choice patterns |
| `{{CHECKLIST_ITEMS}}` | One checklist line per required completion (`- ☐ …`) |

Do **not** put the starter-template line in the student Practice page (instructors track `programming-1` / `programming-2` in Instructor Notes).

## Checklists

Markdown task lists (`- [ ]`) do **not** copy cleanly into Blackboard. Always use the ballot-box emoji instead:

```markdown
- ☐ Completed one Title problem
- ☐ Correct file names
```

Never use `- [ ]` or `- [x]` in Practice pages.

## Choice patterns (pick one)

### A. Sections with OR (choose one per section)

Use when problems group by skill. Each section is an **either/or**: pick **one** problem from that section.

```markdown
### Section K - Title (Choose One)

#### Problem Ka: Name
...
#### Problem Kb: Name
...
```

- Overview / Requirements: `One problem from Section K – Title` (one bullet per section).
- Checklist: `Completed one Title problem` (one line per section).
- File names often use lettered ids (`program1a.py`, `program1b.py`).

### B. Flat choose-N (any N of M)

Use when all problems are peers. No sections. Complete **any N** of the M problems.

```markdown
#### Problem 1: Name
...
#### Problem 2: Name
...
```

- Overview / Requirements: `Any N of the M problems below`.
- Checklist: `Completed N of M problems`.
- File names often use numbered ids (`program1.py`, `program2.py`).

Do **not** require every problem unless the module truly needs that.

## Problem body shape

```markdown
#### Problem …: Name

Intro sentence.

**Requirements:**

- ...

**Rules / Scale:** (when needed)

- ...

**Sample Output:**

\`\`\`text
...
\`\`\`
```

- Keep sample output in a `text` fence.
- Keep published file names stable.
- Reuse the template’s Start Here, AI Disclosure, and Submission blocks; do not invent a second AI disclaimer set.

## Voice and LMS

- Student voice; Blackboard = LMS URL submission.
- Label the accept control **GitHub Classroom Assignment** even when the backend is classroom50.
- Always keep the WARNING: submit the **repository** URL, not Codespaces / `github.dev`.
- No em dashes.

## Sync

After changing how many problems students must complete, update that module’s Overview Practice blurb to match.
